WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.860
If maturing inhibition opens the window, what closes it?

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.880
Does the machinery for change simply wear out?

3
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:15.033
If so, removing one molecule in an adult should not bring the window back.

4
00:00:15.983 --> 00:00:21.443
As the window ends, a lattice of matrix called a perineuronal net condenses around

5
00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:22.883
many parvalbumin cells.

6
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:25.173
Pause and predict.

7
00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:28.993
Digest that net in an adult rat, then close one eye.

8
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:30.833
Does the cortex shift?

9
00:00:37.266 --> 00:00:43.426
It does. Chondroitinase, an enzyme that cuts the net's sugar chains, let deprivation

10
00:00:43.426 --> 00:00:45.166
shift adult rat cortex.

11
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.680
Myelin carries proteins such as Nogo.

12
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:54.240
Mice lacking the Nogo receptor kept plasticity past the usual closing age.

13
00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:59.853
Lynx1 is a small membrane protein that damps nicotinic receptors.

14
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.033
Adult mice without it kept strong plasticity.

15
00:01:04.016 --> 00:01:07.656
Blocking nicotinic receptors prevented that plasticity.

16
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.850
Inhibition itself has a second job.

17
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.770
Past the threshold, it keeps maturing and becomes a brake.

18
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:20.453
In adult rats, reducing GABA transmission partly restored plasticity.

19
00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:26.596
In adult rats, weeks of the antidepressant fluoxetine lowered inhibition and

20
00:01:26.596 --> 00:01:27.816
restored plasticity.

21
00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:29.856
Diazepam blocked that.

22
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.920
In the knockout, diazepam opened the window.

23
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.480
In the adult, it put the brake back.

24
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.743
Now a direct test of whether the window follows the cells.

25
00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:47.703
Transplant embryonic inhibitory neuron precursors into a young mouse's cortex.

26
00:01:48.816 --> 00:01:52.396
They mature into interneurons, including parvalbumin cells.

27
00:01:53.316 --> 00:01:54.636
The host's own window closes.

28
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.450
Pause and predict.

29
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.630
Will a second window come at the host's age, or at the cells' age?

30
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:12.483
The cells' age. When they reached the age of native interneurons in the normal

31
00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:14.643
window, the host shifted again.

32
00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:17.483
Why does this matter?

33
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:23.543
In amblyopia, one eye sees poorly because its input to the cortex was degraded in

34
00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.543
childhood.

35
00:02:25.016 --> 00:02:29.416
Patching the good eye works best in young children, and much less reliably in

36
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:30.416
adults.

37
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.710
These rodent results show mechanism, not treatment.

38
00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.570
Reopening plasticity can also reopen vulnerability.

39
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:44.323
Takeaway: in rodent visual cortex, this window is set by the state of a circuit, not

40
00:02:44.323 --> 00:02:49.623
simply by age. Inhibition opens it, and added brakes, including more mature

41
00:02:49.623 --> 00:02:50.783
inhibition, close it.
